### **A.4 How Powershare Page References Strings**

**Pattern:** Bare string keys resolve implicitly via SwiftUI's `LocalizedStringKey`.

**Examples from PowersharePage.swift (lines 39, 77-80, 98):**
```swift
// Line 39: Direct string key in navigationTitle
.navigationTitle(Text("powershare.title"))

// Line 77: TSPageTitle helper
TSPageTitle("powershare.title")

// Line 78: Direct Text usage
Text("powershare.subtitle")
  .font(Font.TS.body)
  .foregroundStyle(Color.TS.textSecondary)

// Line 98: LocalizedStringKey explicit cast
options: model.vehicles.map { TSSelectOption($0.id, LocalizedStringKey($0.name)) }
```

**Resolution Mechanism:**
- **Bundle/Table:** Default — `Localizable.xcstrings` (app's main localization bundle)
- **No custom wrapper:** Views use bare string keys that SwiftUI automatically converts to `LocalizedStringKey`
- **No explicit `.table()` or `.bundle()`** qualifier is needed; Xcode infers the default

**Confirmation from PowersharePage.Sections.swift (lines 81, 86):**
```swift
